# Clean Architecture Rules

## Layer Dependency Rules

```
PRESENTATION (CLI, GUI, API)
       | depends on
APPLICATION (Use Cases, Application Services)
       | depends on
DOMAIN (Entities, Value Objects, Domain Interfaces)
       ^ implements
INFRASTRUCTURE (ROS2 Adapters, Hardware, Persistence)
```

Critical rules:
1. Domain layer must NOT depend on any outer layer.
2. Application layer can only depend on Domain layer.
3. Infrastructure layer implements Domain interfaces.
4. Presentation layer can only depend on Application layer.

## Domain Layer: Entities

```python
from dataclasses import dataclass
from uuid import UUID, uuid4

@dataclass
class Entity:
    id: UUID = None
    def __post_init__(self):
        if self.id is None:
            self.id = uuid4()

@dataclass
class Robot(Entity):
    name: str
    max_velocity: float
    max_acceleration: float
```

```cpp
namespace domain::entities {
struct Robot {
    std::string id;
    std::string name;
    double max_velocity;
    double max_acceleration;
    bool operator==(const Robot& other) const { return id == other.id; }
};
}
```

## Domain Layer: Value Objects (immutable)

```python
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Position:
    x: float
    y: float
    z: float = 0.0

    def distance_to(self, other: 'Position') -> float:
        return ((self.x - other.x)**2 + (self.y - other.y)**2 + (self.z - other.z)**2) ** 0.5
```

## Domain Interfaces (Ports)

```python
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

class RobotRepository(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def get_by_id(self, robot_id): ...
    @abstractmethod
    def save(self, robot): ...
```

## Application Layer: Use Cases

```python
class MoveRobotUseCase:
    def __init__(self, motion_controller):
        self._motion_controller = motion_controller

    def execute(self, target) -> bool:
        return self._motion_controller.move_to(target)
```

## Infrastructure Layer: ROS2 Adapters

Implements the domain interface, never the reverse.

```python
class ROS2MotionController(MotionController):
    """ROS2 adapter implementing MotionController port."""
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

```python
# WRONG: Domain importing ROS2
from rclpy.node import Node

class Robot(Entity):
    def __init__(self, node: Node):  # WRONG
        self.node = node

# WRONG: Business logic in infrastructure
class ROS2MotionController:
    def move_to(self, position):
        if self.battery_level < 20:  # belongs in domain/application
            return False
```

```cpp
// WRONG: Domain header including ROS2
#include <rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp>
namespace domain::entities {
    class Robot { rclcpp::Node::SharedPtr node_; }; // WRONG
}
```
